@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Round-robin Picker
+
+**Type:** `round-robin-picker`
+
+Selects the next endpoint in a stable lexical order of namespace, pod name,
+address, serving port, and rank. Scores do not affect selection. A mutex
+serializes cursor advances within a plugin instance. For a stable candidate
+set, every endpoint is selected once per cycle, including concurrent calls.
+Completion order of concurrent requests is not selection order.
+
+When candidates change, selection resumes at the first available endpoint
+after the last selected identity, wrapping to the beginning when needed.
+An empty set returns no endpoints and leaves the cursor unchanged. Duplicate
+identities count once. Candidate slices and endpoint metadata remain unchanged.
+
+`maxNumOfEndpoints` defaults to 1. Larger values select a consecutive batch of
+distinct endpoints, capped at the number of available candidates, and advance
+the cursor through that batch. Nonpositive values use the default, matching
+the other picker factories.
+
+State belongs to one configured picker instance in one EPP process. Process
+restarts reset the cursor, separate EPP replicas have independent cursors, and
+there is no globally coordinated order. Configure a separate plugin instance
+for each scheduling profile that requires an independent cycle.
+
+```yaml
+plugins:
+- type: round-robin-picker
+  parameters:
+    maxNumOfEndpoints: 1
+schedulingProfiles:
+- name: default
+  plugins:
+  - pluginRef: round-robin-picker
+```
